> I got the Error message "cleanup_burn: obj lamp not lit"
> then it said: "Program in disorder - perhaps you better #quit"

What version of NetHack are you playing? Were there any unusual
circumstances involving the lamp?

> the first time this happened I saved and it made an error and
> recovered the next time it happened I #quit not realizing it would
> kill my game, and it was such a good character too, why does it tell
> you to #quit when it will destroy your game?

Because it has no way of knowing how severe the bug might be; it knows
that it's not so bad that you can't _possibly_ continue (in which case
the dungeon would collapse), but it knows that its idea of gamestate
doesn't match what it should be and it could be the case that you
_shouldn't_ continue, and advises you accordingly. It's up to you
whether you take its advice; if you've read the Guidebook, you know
what the consequences are.

